# No maze flood on a tick (#84)

Words: [README.md — Words used](../../README.md#words-used-in-this-project).
Copy 1 (copy 2: [docs/GAME_DESIGN.md](../../docs/GAME_DESIGN.md) FAST rule 5).

Board VM is **÷8 (~12.5 MHz)**. A recursive BFS + `_copyMapOpen` (31 arrays)
+ `Array(n).fill().map(()=>Array(m))` **every actor every cell** never
returns from `rAF`. HDMI freezes on the last maze frame with **no ERROR**.
PYTHON / FPGA-SIM still look playable. Empty `finder` → no freeze.

**Do not grow `ENV_DEPTH` 384 or `CSTK` 128** to “make PACORIG fit.” The
T200 is out of room; new bits already fail routing. Author the HTML.
Do **not** add a pathfinding opcode.

**Every-tick chase / flee:** four neighbors of the **existing** map
(MRDO `creepToward`). Treat house/door **`2` as open**. While on a `2`,
prefer **smaller y, then column 13** (door) or they never leave the box
(greedy-toward-player goes down). No maze clone. No `forEach` stamping
ghosts as walls.

**Rare shortest path** (eaten eyes → spawn only, or a tower-defense
place/sell): in-place BFS on the existing map (`_ghostHome`), **once per
event**, not per `rAF`. Do **not** restore `finder` / `_copyMapOpen` —
that is ~36 heap objects before the walk (31 row-arrays + options/start/end)
then more per `push`; PACMAN already holds ~676 of `MAX_OBJ=960` and one
call can `fault 3`. Do **not** run any maze flood on chase/flee. Keep the
maze: split the grid/queue at `ARR_CAP=128` (row arrays + a 3×128 BFS
queue for a 360-cell field). Do **not** shrink the playfield or drop
pathfinding to “fit.” `storage/PACMAN.HTML` = one-step chase + zero-heap
eyes home. `storage/PACORIG.HTML` = original flood; board freezes. Do not
title-gate.

```javascript
// BAD — every ghost, every cell (PACORIG / board freeze)
new_map = _copyMapOpen(map.data);
this.path = map.finder({map:new_map, start:this.coord, end:player.coord});
// GOOD — one step, door 2 walks up out of the house (PACMAN chase)
_ghostStep(map.data, this.coord.x, this.coord.y, player.coord.x, player.coord.y, this.orientation, 0, 1);
```
